 items.waterskin.desc_heal=The waterskin is currently being used to store healing water. The more full the waterskin is, the more you will be instantly healed when drinking from it. You will only drink as much as you need.
 items.waterskin.desc_full=The full waterskin seems to radiate energy, perhaps it can be used to bless another survival item?
 items.waterskin.discover_hint=One of the heroes starts with this item.
+
+
+# Werewolf mod
+items.weapon.melee.claws.name=claws
+items.weapon.melee.claws.desc=Your living weapon. Every 50 kills grant +1 level (+1 minimum, +3 maximum damage). Cannot be unequipped, upgraded, transmuted or enchanted by ordinary means. A claw whetstone rerolls its enchantment without changing its level.
+items.weapon.melee.claws.ac_heart_pierce=Heart-piercing
+items.weapon.melee.claws.ac_pounce=Pounce
+items.weapon.melee.claws.heart_prompt=Select an enemy within claw reach
+items.weapon.melee.claws.pounce_prompt=Select an enemy or a visible landing cell
+items.weapon.melee.claws.no_charge=Not enough charge.
+items.weapon.melee.claws.invalid_target=That target is out of reach or the path is blocked.
+items.weapon.melee.claws.charge_info=Heart-piercing: %s charges. Costs 1; a normal attack with +1-3 damage and bleeding. Charges regenerate over time.
+items.weapon.melee.claws.kills_info=Total hunt kills: _%d_. Growth has no gameplay cap.
+items.weapon.melee.claws.pounce_info=Pounce: %s charges. Costs 1, recharges 1 per 30 turns.
+items.clawwhetstone.name=claw whetstone
+items.clawwhetstone.desc=Rerolls your claw enchantment using the normal enchantment pool, excluding the current enchantment. Preserves all kill upgrades. Craft one with 8 iron scraps and 6 alchemical energy, or earn one every 100 kills.
+items.clawwhetstone.ac_apply=Sharpen
+items.clawwhetstone.prompt=Select your claws
+items.clawwhetstone.applied=Your claws gain a new enchantment.
+items.ironscraps.name=iron scraps
+items.ironscraps.desc=Recovered from dismantled weapons. Yield: weapon tier + one scrap per two positive upgrades, per weapon. Craft a claw whetstone using 8 scraps and 6 alchemical energy.
+items.kindofweapon.ac_dismantle=Dismantle
+items.kindofweapon.dismantled=Recovered %d iron scraps.
+items.kindofweapon.claws_only=A werewolf fights only with claws.
+items.food.food.ac_open=Open
+items.food.food.opened=The ration contained %d pieces of raw meat.
+items.food.food.cannot_eat=Open the ration to take out its meat.
+items.food.food.werewolf_desc=Werewolves cannot eat this ration directly. Open it in one turn for 1 or 2 raw meats, with equal probability.
+items.food.pasty.werewolf_desc=A werewolf can eat this, but it restores only one hunger band (150). It uses the same five-way raw-meat roll: burning, rooting, poison, slow, or no side effect. Fire and freezing do not make it safe.
+items.food.pasty.meat_portion=You found and ate the meat filling.
+items.food.mysterymeat.werewolf_desc=Fresh meat. Werewolves suffer no raw-meat side effects and eat it in one turn.
+items.armor.werewolfarmor.name=werewolf armor
+items.armor.werewolfarmor.desc=Royal armor shaped for a hunter. It fuels Beast Rampage. The werewolf's normal armor penalty remains in effect.
diff --git a/core/src/main/assets/messages/items/items_ko.properties b/core/src/main/assets/messages/items/items_ko.properties
